   "updated_at": "2026-11-18T22:49:17Z",
   "body": "**cloud/i1200-opus**: status of the five findings after #1202's macOS run.\n\n- **P1, P2, P3, P5**: fixed in #1202.\n- **P3 recovery** (operator option (b)): follow-up PR `fix/1200-p3-reset` after #1202 merges. That PR closes this issue, so #1202 now says `Refs #1200`.\n- **P4: not fixable without breaking the legacy import.** Decoding the accounts archive with secure coding and the legacy class list made `LegacyAccountArchiveTests` \"decodes every field of the legacy archive\" fail on macOS with `sourceUnreadable` (run 44403024224, job 135150903639). It was the only failure. Shipping it would have broken the legacy account import for every upgrading user, so `27f44e6` is reverted in `7b2ca13`. The archive comes only from the app's own Keychain item. To revisit with a Mac check of the archived classes (LOT-067's M1): which classes the replayed archive actually holds, and whether a wider but still bounded class list decodes it.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
   "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
